# Feature (negative): an UNANNOTATED literal defaults to platform `int`, whose value must
# still fit a 64-bit word. 2^64 is past `uint64`'s max, so no `iconst` can hold it — it is
# rejected at the checker (T0034) rather than escaping to a codegen-time note.
fn main() -> int {
    x := 18446744073709551616
    return 0
}
# expect: compile-error "out of range"
